{"task_id": "HumanEval/21", "solution": "from typing import List\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input.\"\"\"\n    pass\ndef rescale_to_unit(numbers: List[float]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\" Given list of numbers, apply a linear transform so the smallest number becomes 0 and the largest becomes 1.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if the input list contains fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list must contain at least two elements.\")\n\n    min_val = min(numbers)\n    max_val = max(numbers)\n\n    if max_val == min_val:\n        # All numbers are identical, rescale to 0.0\n        return [0.0] * len(numbers)\n    else:\n        scale_factor = 1.0 / (max_val - min_val)\n        return [(x - min_val) * scale_factor for x in numbers]"}
