{"task_id": "HumanEval/60", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input values.\n    It carries a descriptive message about the validation failure.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\ndef sum_to_n(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of numbers from 1 to n.\n    It raises `InvalidInputError` if `n` is not a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Parameter 'n' must be an integer, but got {type(n).__name__}.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Parameter 'n' must be a positive integer, but got {n}.\")\n    \n    return n * (n + 1) // 2"}
