{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three,\n    while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    third_indices_values = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            third_indices_values.append(l[i])\n\n    third_indices_values.sort()\n\n    result_list = l[:]  # Create a shallow copy of the original list.\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            result_list[i] = third_indices_values[sorted_idx]\n            sorted_idx += 1\n            \n    return result_list"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not all(isinstance(item, (int, float)) for item in l):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n    if not l:\n        return None\n\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2"}
